> > > the weakest and the toughest monsters that would be generated.
> >
> > It's the average of your XL and the dungeon level.  Since archons are
> > (I think) about level 20, even if you're only level 1 by level 39
> > they'll be common.
> 
> Once you hit the sanctum, the number used to generate monsters
> hits its max, and it never goes down from that point on.

Not quite; there are three distinct phases which use different values
for the DL component of monster selection:

Before acquiring the Amulet: DL = your actual DL
After acquiring the Amulet: DL = Sanctum DL
In the Endgame: DL = Sanctum DL + XL/2

> So while protectionist can cause weaker monsters to be generated
> until then, the result is a smaller possible pool of weak monsters
> after you get the Amulet.

The cut-off at the bottom end of the range depends solely on the DL
component, not the XL, so your XL will only make a difference to it in
the Endgame; at which point random as opposed to preplaced monster
generation is a fairly minor factor.

